# AOM Adda

Railway AOM exam-prep site. Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS 4, Mongoose, Zod, jose sessions, lucide-react. Import via `@/` (project root).

## Next.js 16

This is not the Next.js from training data. Before writing framework code, read the matching guide in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` and heed deprecation notices.

- App Router only (`app/`). Routes live under `/topics`, `/manuals`, `/acts`, `/quizzes`, `/general-awareness`, `/pdfs`, `/api`.
- Server Components by default. Add `'use client'` only when the file needs client APIs.
- Use `next/link` for navigation and `NextResponse` in route handlers.

## New public pages

When adding a public page, also add a `SearchTopic` in `lib/search-topics.ts`:

```ts
{
  href: "/topics/example",
  title: "Example",
  category: "Study Topics",
  parent: "Topics",
  keywords: "topics example Example extra search words",
}
```

Place it alphabetically by `title` among nearby entries. Do not skip the search index.

## Auth and APIs

- Sessions: `lib/auth/session.ts` (jose JWT cookie). Models: `lib/models/`. DB: `lib/db.ts`.
- Validate request bodies with Zod in `lib/validations`. Return `{ error, fieldErrors }` on 400.
- Keep public paths in `middleware.ts` (`PUBLIC_PAGE_PATHS`, `PUBLIC_API_PREFIXES`) when adding unauthenticated routes.

## Style

- Match the file you are editing (quotes, exports, component shape).
- Do not mass-refactor the large generated trees under `components/` (manuals, acts, chapter/section pages).
- Do not commit `.env` or secrets.
